<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ibid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "[International Business Identifier (IBID)](https://ekys.org/business_identifiers/) is a verifiable unique identifier for legal entities as defined in the [ISO/DIS 25500-3](https://www.iso.org/standard/87705.html) draft standard. It is composed of three data elements: the International Business Registration Number (IBRN), the legal name, and the date of origin formatted as eight numeric characters (YYYYMMDD). Each element is separated by a pipe character (`|`) (e.g., `US-DE.BER:3031657|Code Management Association|19990420`)."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/requirementUUID> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "requirementUUID" .
_:N1ed768e70d8d4776bb6cda626836c6cc <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:Nd88b8b2c15f34dddb3b904b251ea678e .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ibrn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "[International Business Registration Number (IBRN)](https://ekys.org/business_identifiers/) is a unique identifier for legal entities standardized by [ISO 8000-116](https://www.iso.org/standard/75117.html). It is composed of two parts: a jurisdiction prefix and a local authoritative legal entity identifier (ALEI), separated by a colon. The prefix contains an ISO 3166 country code, an optional subdivision code, and a register code (e.g., `US-DE.BER:3031657`)."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/FunctionalSafety/evaluationBasedOn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates the specific RequirementVerification instance on which the EvaluationResult is based."@en .
